\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Our day of praise is done,
\par The evening shadows fall;
\par But pass not from us with 
\par the sun,
\par True Light, that lightenest all!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Around the throne on high,
\par Where night can never be,
\par The white- robed harpers of the sky
\par Bring ceaseless hymns to Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Too faint our anthems here;
\par Too soon of praise we tire;
\par But O the strains, how full and clear,
\par Of that eternal choir!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Yet, Lord, to Thy dear will,
\par If Thou attune the heart,
\par We in Thine angels' music still
\par May bear our lower part.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. 'Tis Thine each soul to claim,
\par Each wayward thought reclaim,
\par And make our life a daily psalm
\par Of glory to Thy name.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. A little while, and then
\par Shall come the glorious end,
\par And songs of angels and of men
\par In perfect praise shall blend.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

